<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ DAY 1 -->
<!-- day-count: 3 — Alcatraz is a half-day / time-intensive anchor (round-trip ferry + cellhouse audio tour runs ~2.5–3h), so the afternoon is given to it; Ferry Building and Coit Tower fill the morning -->
<div class="day-block" id="day1">
  <div class="day-header">Day 1</div>

  <div class="hotel-first">🏨 FROM HOTEL: 🚶 5 min · 🚕  3 min → Ferry Building Marketplace</div>

  <!-- inclusion-bar: editorial — Fodor's, SF Travel, Atlas Obscura name the Ferry Building as the city's defining waterfront landmark and a Beaux-Arts National Register site -->
  <div class="stop-block">
    <div class="stop-header"><span class="stop-num">1.</span> <span class="stop-name self">Ferry Building Marketplace</span></div>
    <div class="stop-row">📒 Beaux-Arts ferry terminal opened 1898, restored 2003 as a living food hall — nearly 50 artisan vendors, oyster bars, bread counters, and farmers-market stalls under the 245-foot clock tower. The city's iconic gateway from the Bay.</div>
    <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Ferry_Building" target="_blank">Wikipedia</a></div>
    <div class="tour-box">
      <div>🏛️ Daily 7:00am - 10:00pm</div>
      <div>⏰ ~1h 30 min</div>
      <div class="tour-meet"><div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ferry+Building+1+Ferry+Building+San+Francisco+CA+94111" target="_blank">1 Ferry Building</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <!-- photo-ok: Ferry Building is itself the architectural attraction — the Beaux-Arts facade with clock tower is the iconic shot -->
    <div class="stop-photos">
      <img src="_build/assets/800px-Ferry_Building_San_Francisco.jpg" alt="Ferry Building">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="next">🚶 16 min · 🚕  6 min → Coit Tower</div>

  <!-- inclusion-bar: editorial — Fodor's, Rick Steves SF, NPS, Atlas Obscura — landmark architecture + significant 1933 Depression-era murals + panoramic viewpoint -->
  <div class="stop-block">
    <div class="stop-header"><span class="stop-num">2.</span> <span class="stop-name self">Coit Tower</span></div>
    <div class="stop-row">📒 A 210-foot concrete column on the summit of Telegraph Hill, completed 1933 from a public bequest. Inside, sweeping Depression-era frescoes by 25 muralists circle the lobby; outside, the parapet gives a 360° panorama from Alcatraz to the Bay Bridge.</div>
    <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coit_Tower" target="_blank">Wikipedia</a></div>
    <div class="tour-box">
      <div>🏛️ Daily 10:00am - 6:00pm</div>
      <div>⏰ ~1h</div>
      <div class="tour-meet"><div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Coit+Tower+1+Telegraph+Hill+Blvd+San+Francisco+CA+94133" target="_blank">1 Telegraph Hill Blvd</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="stop-photos">
      <img src="_build/assets/800px-Coit_tower.jpg" alt="Coit Tower">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="next">🚶 16 min · 🚕  7 min → Alcatraz Island</div>

  <!-- inclusion-bar: editorial — NPS, Fodor's, Rick Steves, SF Travel — the world-famous former federal penitentiary, one of SF's defining attractions -->
  <!-- tour-search: Alcatraz Island access is sold only through the official NPS concessioner Alcatraz City Cruises departing Pier 33 — booked direct here; Viator / GetYourGuide / TripAdvisor resell the same ferry and appear in the Tours section -->
  <div class="stop-block">
    <div class="stop-header"><span class="stop-num">3.</span> <span class="stop-name self">Alcatraz Island</span></div>
    <div class="stop-row">📒 The rock in the middle of the Bay — military fortress, lighthouse, and federal penitentiary that held Al Capone. The cellhouse audio tour, narrated by former guards and inmates, walks D-Block, the dining hall, and the recreation yard.</div>
    <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcatraz_Island" target="_blank">Wikipedia</a></div>
    <div class="ticket-box">
      <div>🎟️ <a href="https://www.cityexperiences.com/san-francisco/city-cruises/alcatraz/tour-options/alcatraz-day-tour/" target="_blank"><strong>Alcatraz City Cruises</strong></a></div>
      <div>🏛️ Daily 8:40am - 3:50pm</div>
      <div>⏰ ~2h 30 min</div>
      <div class="tour-meet"><div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pier+33+Alcatraz+Landing+San+Francisco+CA+94133" target="_blank">Pier 33 Alcatraz Landing</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="stop-photos">
      <img src="_build/assets/800px-Alcatraz_Island_photo_Don_Ramey_Logan.jpg" alt="Alcatraz Island">
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- walk-over-40: Pier 33 to hotel walk is around 28 min along the Embarcadero — ride is faster at day end -->
  <div class="next">🚕  8 min → hotel</div>
</div>

